  "description": "Model spec midtraining (Li et al., 2026, arXiv 2605.02087) at about the paper's smaller data setting (8M tokens of documents), for recursive_oct/msm.py. Documents: the authors' six prompts verbatim (prompts/msm/), written by the untrained model with reasoning off; the writer chooses the domains and subdomains, each subdomain gets 10 document types, and the ideas per type are set to give about 3,500 documents (the authors' run used 20 types x 25 ideas for 41M tokens). Training follows the paper's appendix B.4: LoRA rank 64, alpha 128, every linear layer, one epoch, AdamW at 1e-4 with a cosine schedule, 5% warmup, weight decay 0.01, for both midtraining and AFT. AFT: the reasoning teacher's answers to the round's trait prompts (5 per prompt) plus the untrained model's own answers to the general prompts (2 per prompt).",
